      "worked": "The horizontal factor is $\\frac{1}{h}$, so replace $x\\mapsto \\frac{x}{(\\frac{1}{h})}=hx$. For the vertical factor, replace $y\\mapsto \\frac{y}{k}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{y}{k}&=(hx)^2\\\\y&=kh^2x^2\\\\kh^2&=100\\\\k&=\\frac{100}{h^2}\\end{align*}$$\nFor $k$ to be a positive integer, $h^2$ must divide $100=2^2\\times5^2$. Thus $h$ can only be $1,2,5$ or $10$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(h,k)&=(10,1),\\ (5,4),\\ (2,25),\\ (1,100)\\end{align*}$$",
